The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>if (ret)
    return ret;</text>
<text>if (ret) {
    of_node_put(ulpi->dev.of_node);
    return ret;
}</text>
Reason:
These error paths in `ulpi_register()` do not free the allocated `ulpi` structure when `ulpi_of_register()` or `ulpi_read_id()` fail before `device_register()` is called. A prior fix removed `kfree(ulpi)` from another function to prevent double-free when `device_register()` fails, but it inadvertently caused this memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>if (ret) {
    kfree(ulpi);
    return ret;
}</text>
<text>if (ret) {
    of_node_put(ulpi->dev.of_node);
    kfree(ulpi);
    return ret;
}</text>
Reason:
Adding `kfree(ulpi)` on both early error paths ensures the allocated memory is properly freed before returning, preventing the leak. This is consistent with the memory ownership: `ulpi` is allocated in the caller and should be freed if registration fails before the device is registered.

